// =============================================================================
// logging.json — which log levels are written to other/logging/app/
// =============================================================================
// Location (dev):     <repo>/other/configs/logging.json
// Location (install): <folder next to the .exe>/other/configs/logging.json
//
// How to use:
//   1. Set each level to true (include) or false (exclude) and save.
//   2. Changes apply automatically while the app is running (file watcher).
//   3. Unknown keys are ignored; missing keys fall back to defaults.
//   4. Comments (// and /* */) are allowed — this is JSONC, not strict JSON.
//
// Levels map to the Rust `log` crate except `fatal`, which is a separate
// channel (error-level messages tagged with target gensource::fatal).
// Build logs under other/logging/build/ are full transcripts and ignore this file.
// =============================================================================
{
  "error": true,
  "warn": true,
  "info": true,
  "debug": false,
  "trace": false,
  "fatal": true
}
